    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean, additive, and consistent with the established conventions of this codebase.\n\n- **Soundex lives in the right unit.** `Owner.soundex(...)` is placed alongside the other static, deterministic derived-value helpers (`identityKey`, `householdId`, `customerCode`, `normalizeTelephone`, `normalizeEmail`), keeping the model as the single source of truth for derived identity components. The service layer (`assertIdentityIsUnique`, `assignPossibleDuplicate`) continues to own the business-rule orchestration. The hard/soft duplicate split stays where it belongs.\n\n- **The lookup table is co-located sensibly.** `SOUNDEX_CODES` and its static initializer sit directly above their sole consumer `soundex(...)`, which matches the local convention of placing constants next to the method that uses them (e.g. `FISCAL_YEAR_START_MONTH`).\n\n- **Hand-rolling Soundex is idiomatic here.** The codebase already hand-rolls its hashing primitive (`sha256Hex`) rather than pulling in a library, so an in-house Soundex is the natural, consistent choice rather than an external dependency.\n\n- **No dead code left behind.** `householdId(...)` remains legitimately used by `countHouseholdMembers`, `computeMembershipLevel`, and `OwnerMapper.formatHouseholdId`, so dropping it from the identity key did not orphan it. The old 4-arg `identityKey` signature was cleanly collapsed to 3 args at every call site (mapper, service, exception, and javadoc `@link`s), and the OpenAPI schema and all surrounding javadoc were updated to match.\n\n- **No new catch-all or duplication of concern.** The repeated `Owner.identityKey(existing...)` computation across the two stream pipelines mirrors the pre-existing per-check stream style in this class (each guard builds its own filtered stream over `findAll()`), so it reads as consistent rather than as copy-paste that should be extracted.\n\nA maintainer of this repository would find the result natural.",
